---LINES

mainv   = gh  - - - - "main view"
mainvk  = g  - - - - "main view keys:"

cmded   = gh  - - - - "command editor"
cmdedk  = g  - - - - "command editor keys:"

exit    = gh  - - - - "exit trap"
exitk   = g  - - - - "keys of trap on exit:"

hist    = gh  - - - - "history view"
histk   = g  - - - - "history view keys:"

runcmd  = gh  - - - - "run a command"

---# m       = gm  - - - - " *)"
m       = g  - - - - " *)"

cmd     = ghx - - - -  "[a-z./]"
CMD     = ghx - - - -  "[A-Z0-9]"

---SCREEN
=vash workflow                                      
+                                      please, see 'man vash' for more details       
+.mainvk.................................                                     
+ .'lowercase or .'. or .'/                 exit:                       help:   
+    - type a command from scratch    {1}   .:EX...                     .:HE... 
+ .'other                                   .mainv............................. 
+    - edit a command from template   {2}    ^  .:CA          .cmd...  .CMD.... 
+    - execute predefined command     {3}    :  ^:                 :    :    :  
+ .:CA - switch to editor                    :  ::  ."history".   {1}  {2}  {3} 
+                                            :  ::    ^ .:NL...    :    :    :  
+.cmdedk.................................    :  ::    :     :      :    :    :  
+  .:NL...  - run a command, sync history    : .:CA .:HE... :      :    :    :  
+  .:HE...  - switch to history view         : .cmded.....................   :  
+                                            :      ^              .:NL...   :  
+.histk..................................    :      :                  :     :  
+  .:NL...  - take a command to editor       :     {1}       .runcmd.......... 
+  .:CA     - return to editor untouched    .:CA    :        :
+                                           .:SP... .cmd...  :                  
+.exitk..................................   .exit.............                  
+  .:CA, .:SP... - return to main view        .:NL... --> trap                       
+  type a command - return to editor                                            
                                                                                
---END                                                                         
+  .:NL...  - defencive trap for mistakes   
+                                     .m. see 'man vash' for details

